<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:53:32 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>‘A more expensive EU is not a better EU’: Austria's Minister for Europe, Claudia Bauer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-a-more-expensive-eu-is-not-a-better-eu-austria-s-minister-for-europe-claudia-bauer</link><description>
This week's programme hosted Claudia Bauer, Austria’s Federal Minister for Europe, Integration and Family while she was in Paris for the recent G7 meeting. She offered her thoughts on the diplomatic moves surrounding Ukraine, transatlantic relations, EU enlargement and a headscarf ban in Austrian schools that has caused disquiet. We also talked about the thorny negotiations involved in the EU’s next long-term budget: the Multiannual Financial Framework.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ec2d102-e355-11f1-9179-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-CLAUDIA-BAUER-TALKING-EUROPE-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2ec2d102-e355-11f1-9179-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-CLAUDIA-BAUER-TALKING-EUROPE-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc86b92a-e1a8-11f1-864d-8d7f3ec53496</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:53:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Spain’s political crossroads, Europe’s wider stakes: Spaniards to vote in key election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election</link><description>
The stakes are high – not only for people in Spain, but also for Europe. On November 29, the country holds a parliamentary election that could see the end of the Socialist-led government and potentially a coalition between the right and the far right, in one of the EU’s biggest and most influential member states. It could also signal the end of Pedro Sanchez’s third term in office. Among other things, the prime minister may pay the political price for two shocking train crashes and the migrant crisis in Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb70dc0a-e434-11f1-8bdf-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-SPAIN-DEBATE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb70dc0a-e434-11f1-8bdf-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/TALKING-EUROPE-SPAIN-DEBATE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64fa5a54-e1a9-11f1-b476-43a8f9a2efe8</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:17:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>Does staggered consent actually protect young people?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people</link><description>
Following recent scandals involving two iconic British comedians, the UK government is considering the introduction of staggered age consent. Annette Young talks to Katherine Allen from the Institute of Social Justice and Crime in the UK about whether such laws work. Also the social costs of femicide; how do loved ones cope with such a loss, and what support is available to families in the wake of such a tragedy? Plus we meet the women who are challenging the traditions of Mexican mariachi music, a world that remains largely male dominated. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75df6f36-e4e6-11f1-8b81-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75df6f36-e4e6-11f1-8b81-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/51-PERCENT-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3cd92630-e4ca-11f1-a1e0-39177940782c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:14:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland's Tusk denounces Russian 'provocation' after Warsaw says missile hit territory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-poland-says-russian-missile-hit-its-territory-during-attack-on-ukraine</link><description>
Poland on Friday said that no one was hurt after what Warsaw alleged was a Russian missile hit southeast Poland during an attack on Ukraine. Polish authorities earlier said they were investigating reports that at ​least two unknown objects had fallen near the border with Ukraine. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0215cd4e-e4cc-11f1-ba35-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T091417Z-724863669-RC2KROAVQTVB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-POLAND-OBJECTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0215cd4e-e4cc-11f1-ba35-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T091417Z-724863669-RC2KROAVQTVB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-POLAND-OBJECTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a2669722-e4c9-11f1-a9b0-77b31efc897d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:38:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0215cd4e-e4cc-11f1-ba35-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T091417Z-724863669-RC2KROAVQTVB-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-POLAND-OBJECTS.jpg">© Kacper Pempel, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe's youth set to join mass cost of living protests in 25 countries</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-europe-s-youth-set-to-join-mass-cost-of-living-protests-in-25-countries</link><description>
Youth protests are set to take place in more than 25 countries in Europe on Friday and over the weekend, coalition organisers said, as demostrators seek to increase pressure on governments over issues including soaring housing costs and deteriorating learning conditions with a show of cross-border solidarity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c479d6d8-e4b7-11f1-9b6e-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321479139816.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c479d6d8-e4b7-11f1-9b6e-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321479139816.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cb122d10-e4b7-11f1-9b30-8f0cacea5e64</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:57:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c479d6d8-e4b7-11f1-9b6e-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321479139816.jpg">© Aurelien Morissard, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: France seeks UN Security Council meeting after Russian strikes hit European embassies in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-live-deadly-russian-attacks-damage-two-bridges-in-kyiv-mayor-says</link><description>
France called for a UN Security Council meeting following a salvo of Russian strikes on Ukraine Friday that damaged the Austrian and Dutch embassies in Kyiv, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said. The fresh wave of missile and drone attacks came after Russian President Vladimir Putin vowed a "painful" retaliation after Ukraine this week damaged the Crimea bridge. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc4e63e4-e4c5-11f1-bd73-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T090314Z-647512984-RC2LROAKCHGW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc4e63e4-e4c5-11f1-bd73-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T090314Z-647512984-RC2LROAKCHGW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c85c9ea-e4ab-11f1-a114-d3a799165f5c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:32:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc4e63e4-e4c5-11f1-bd73-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T090314Z-647512984-RC2LROAKCHGW-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Thomas Peter, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA[Czechs protest en masse against concentration of power & feared government control over public media]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-czechs-protest-en-masse-against-concentration-of-power-in-one-hand-and-growing-control-over-media</link><description>
As large demonstrations in the Czech Republic challenge Prime Minister Andrej Babiš's plans to change the funding model of public broadcasters, Mikuláš Minář, Chair of the Million Moments for Democracy movement, joins François Picard from Prague for Spotlight, warning that his country risks following Hungary and Slovakia in democratic backsliding. "We are really afraid that the Czech Republic is following the Orbánian Hungarian way, (Fico's) Slovakian way," he says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4a816a9a-e4a7-11f1-87a2-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e133a2a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8a83266-e4a7-11f1-b6fc-0f49ce47132d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:02:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Burnham hails 'landmark' EU-UK deal on trade, youth mobility as 'good day' for Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-eu-and-uk-set-to-sign-deals-on-trade-energy-youth-mobility-at-brussels-summit</link><description>
The United Kingdom and European Union agreed to a new deal on trade, energy and youth mobility on Friday, which UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham called a "good day" for both London and the bloc. Burnham – who has said he hopes to see Britain rejoin the EU in his lifetime – argues the deals will help fix some of the damage Brexit inflicted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbd676e-e4e6-11f1-937b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132734Z-1827993248-RC2OROAYAMFA-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT-BURNHAM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbd676e-e4e6-11f1-937b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132734Z-1827993248-RC2OROAYAMFA-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT-BURNHAM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">215366b2-e486-11f1-8392-c54bec5a97cd</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:00:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fdbd676e-e4e6-11f1-937b-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-20T132734Z-1827993248-RC2OROAYAMFA-RTRMADP-3-EU-BRITAIN-SUMMIT-BURNHAM.jpg">© Hannah McKay, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>PM Sanchez admits 'mistakes' in key debate ahead of Spain's election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-pm-s%C3%A1nchez-admits-mistakes-in-key-debate-ahead-of-spain-election</link><description>
Spain's Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez acknowledged shortcomings in his government on Thursday as he faced conservative rival Alberto Nunez Feijoo in the campaign's only televised debate. The November 29 election could leave the far-right Vox party in a position to enter government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">47a90c40-e47c-11f1-823f-bb1d3788691b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:49:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adb0ecfc-e435-11f1-9ff1-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/bfcd4adc17d0c1b4d4952e5c826ecffd1efc0af3.jpg">© Jaime Reina, Josep Lago, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russian strikes on Kyiv kill one, damage Dutch and Austrian embassies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russian-strikes-on-kyiv-kill-one-damage-dutch-and-austrian-embassies</link><description>
A wave of daytime Russian strikes on Kyiv on Thursday killed one person and damaged a historic cathedral as well as the embassies of Austria and the Netherlands. Loud explosions erupted across the Ukraine capital throughout the day as the leaders of Russia, China and the United States held a historic meeting in China that put Russia's President Vladimir Putin in international spotlight. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58fdce58-e45f-11f1-99b5-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-203931-204127-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/58fdce58-e45f-11f1-99b5-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-203931-204127-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5eb9e890-e45f-11f1-ab0f-8dbb507a1f19</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:25:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kushner says Trump 'open' to extend NATO mutual defense-type clause to Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kushner-says-trump-open-to-extend-nato-mutual-defense-type-clause-to-ukraine</link><description>
US envoy Jared Kushner said Thursday that President Donald Trump was open to extending to Ukraine a security guarantee similar to NATO's mutual defense clause, but stressed that Washington has to protect its interests too. The comments came as German Chancellor Friedrich Merz qualified the summit between the presidents of the United States, Russia and China as a "photo op". FRANCE 24's international affairs commentator Douglas Herbert explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25b84e6c-e444-11f1-a13d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T175030Z-1149809636-RC24ROAX76LX-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25b84e6c-e444-11f1-a13d-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T175030Z-1149809636-RC24ROAX76LX-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e2b59d8-e452-11f1-b9df-1b5e5e3e7684</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:41:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron urges Ukraine's allies to 'reopen the question' of NATO membership</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-macron-urges-ukraine-allies-reopen-question-nato-membership</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday called for Ukraine's allies to speed up the delivery of urgently needed air defence systems and urged them to "reopen the question" of Ukraine's NATO membership after talks in Berlin aimed at reaffirming European support for Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4326a9aa-e456-11f1-8321-2f542a93f4a9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:32:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1caca7f6-e44d-11f1-80ec-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T181939Z-2056306323-RC23ROA5DSK2-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-GERMANY-BRITAIN.jpg">© Hannah McKay, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Three of a kind? Xi hosts Trump and Putin as Ukraine war grinds on</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261119-three-of-a-kind-xi-hosts-trump-and-putin-as-ukraine-war-grinds-on</link><description>
Gang of three or glorified photo op? Chinese President Xi Jinping is hosting his US and Russian counterparts Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the APEC summit. Already, our Monday panel rejected attempts to paint the three-way meeting as a new Yalta, in reference to the 1945 sit-down on the Black Sea that defined the post-war security architecture of Europe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cf1dff8-e44b-11f1-81ed-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T112415Z-149699658-RC2ZQOAH0BR6-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1cf1dff8-e44b-11f1-81ed-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-19T112415Z-149699658-RC2ZQOAH0BR6-RTRMADP-3-APEC-SUMMIT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c65e57fc-e44a-11f1-91b0-ff7f8e5d3944</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:39:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Behind the UK's use of AI in asylum applications</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/behind-the-uk-s-use-of-ai-in-asylum-applications</link><description>
The UK is increasingly turning to artificial intelligence to manage its immigration system, from analysing migrants’ phones to processing asylum applications. But what happens when AI gets involved in deciding how an asylum seeker's story is understood? Stella Elgersma, journalist at InfoMigrants, explains how the UK Home Office is testing AI tools to process asylum applications, including a system that generates summaries of asylum interviews. With errors, limited human oversight and concerns over transparency, could AI put asylum seekers’ lives at risk?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e36442a-e428-11f1-a386-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-143639-144049-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e36442a-e428-11f1-a386-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-143639-144049-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33d74b0e-e428-11f1-8380-35699edb96b7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:07:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin</link><description>
The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf9490a-e41f-11f1-8a6b-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-140128-140711-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edf9490a-e41f-11f1-8a6b-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-140128-140711-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3513e08-e41f-11f1-ae06-0db31b1ab018</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:04:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine's European allies meet in Berlin in show of support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-s-european-allies-meet-in-berlin-in-show-of-support</link><description>
Ukraine’s main European allies are meeting in Berlin on Thursday as a show of support for Kyiv, with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner also attending. The gathering, which brings together the leaders of Germany, France, Britain, Poland and Italy as well as NATO chief Mark Rutte, takes place as Trump and Putin meet in China, fuelling fears in Europe that decisions on the war could be made without its input. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Germany has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3999d8f4-e21b-11f1-8b8b-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316805802362.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b8491ffc-e400-11f1-9722-0f0809d6071d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:43:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Denmark ratifies Greenland security deal after months of pressure by Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261119-denmark-ratifies-greenland-security-deal-after-months-of-pressure-by-trump</link><description>
Denmark's parliament on Thursday ratified a security deal involving Greenland and the United States. The vote comes months after the US, Denmark and Greenland ​signed the ‌agreement to end a standoff with the Trump administration over the Arctic island's future. 
